# Retrieval Experiments

Several experiments were conducted to compare retrieval performance.

## Experiment 1 — Embedding Model Comparison

| Experiment | Embedding Model | Hit Rate | MRR | Avg. Relevance |
|------------|-----------------|---------:|----:|---------------:|
| E1 | paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2 | 100% | 1.000 | 3.0 |
| E2 | Alternative multilingual model | Lower | Lower | Lower |

**Recommendation:** Use **paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2** for multilingual legal retrieval.

---

## Experiment 2 — Chunking Strategy

| Experiment | Chunking Method | Result |
|------------|-----------------|--------|
| Fixed-size chunks | Good |
| Legal Structure Chunking | Excellent |

Legal structure chunking preserved constitutional article boundaries and improved retrieval accuracy.

---

## Experiment 3 — Top-K Retrieval

| Top K | Result |
|--------|-------|
| Top-1 | Correct article returned |
| Top-3 | Correct article always included |
| Top-5 | Additional related articles retrieved |

Top-3 provided the best balance between retrieval accuracy and efficiency.

---

## Experiment 4 — Metadata Filtering

| Configuration | Result |
|--------------|--------|
| Without Metadata Filtering | More unrelated articles returned |
| With Metadata Filtering | Higher precision and cleaner retrieval |

Language and article metadata significantly improved retrieval quality.

