# Limitations

Although retrieval performance was excellent, several limitations remain.

## OCR Errors

- Low-quality PDF scans may introduce OCR mistakes.
- Incorrect characters can reduce embedding quality.

## Amharic Recognition

- Some Amharic words have multiple spellings.
- Embedding models may not fully capture linguistic nuances.

## Legal Structure Preservation

- Poor chunk boundaries may split related legal provisions.
- Larger legal sections sometimes lose contextual continuity.

## Data Cleaning Risks

- Aggressive preprocessing may remove meaningful legal terminology.

## Embedding Limitations

- General multilingual embedding models are not specifically trained on Ethiopian legal texts.

## Similarity Scores

- High similarity scores do not always guarantee legal relevance.
- Keyword-based re-ranking remains necessary.

## Unsupported Questions

- The system currently relies on similarity thresholds and keyword interception.
- More advanced intent classification could improve unsupported-question detection.

## Corpus Coverage

- Only the FDRE Constitution is indexed.
- Civil Code, Criminal Code, Family Code, and other legal documents are not yet included.

## Infrastructure Limitations

- Vector database size and embedding computation increase memory usage.
- Large legal collections may require optimization for faster retrieval.

